hPC88PL"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0605e517a21a474d016ae20cb9d654819197b4a62fac535401","call_id":"call_ca250e1adb1c4dd995c934a8a33dc2fe","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"spec\":{\"format_version\":2,\"case_id\":\"lie-module-irreducibility\",\"full_target\":\"Let \\\\(p\\\\) be any prime, \\\\(K\\\\) any field of characteristic \\\\(p\\\\), and\\n\\\\(\\\\lambda\\\\) an integer with \\\\(0\\\\leq\\\\lambda<p\\\\).\\nLet \\\\(V(\\\\lambda)\\\\) be the complex irreducible highest-weight\\n\\\\(\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2(\\\\mathbb C)\\\\)-module of highest weight \\\\(\\\\lambda\\\\),\\nof dimension \\\\(\\\\lambda+1\\\\). Its Chevalley generators satisfy\\n\\n\\\\[\\n[h,x]=2x,\\\\qquad[h,y]=-2y,\\\\qquad[x,y]=h.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nChoose a nonzero highest-weight vector \\\\(v\\\\) with \\\\(xv=0\\\\) and\\n\\\\(hv=\\\\lambda v\\\\). Let \\\\(U_{\\\\mathbb Z}\\\\) be the integer subalgebra of\\nthe universal enveloping algebra generated by all divided powers\\n\\\\(X_r=x^r/r!\\\\), \\\\(Y_r=y^r/r!\\\\), for integers \\\\(r\\\\geq0\\\\).\\nAn **admissible lattice** \\\\(M\\\\subset V(\\\\lambda)\\\\) is a free abelian\\nsubgroup with an integer basis that is also a complex basis, stable under\\n\\\\(U_{\\\\mathbb Z}\\\\). It is arbitrary, not necessarily the minimal lattice.\\n\\nPut \\\\(V(K)=M\\\\otimes_{\\\\mathbb Z}K\\\\). The Lie algebra\\n\\\\(L(K)=(\\\\mathbb Zx+\\\\mathbb Zy+\\\\mathbb Zh)\\\\otimes_{\\\\mathbb Z}K\\\\)\\nacts by the induced lattice operators. This is the Chevalley\\n\\\\(\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2\\\\) construction also in characteristic 2.\\nProve that \\\\(V(K)\\\\) is nonzero and every \\\\(K\\\\)-linear subspace\\ninvariant under \\\\(x,y,h\\\\) is zero or all of \\\\(V(K)\\\\).\\nBoth \\\\(\\\\lambda=0\\\\) and \\\\(p=2\\\\) are included; \\\\(K\\\\) need not be\\nalgebraically closed.\",\"conclusion\":\"V(K) is nonzero, and for every K-linear subspace W of V(K), if W is invariant under the induced operators x,y,h then W={0} or W=V(K). Equivalently V(K) is a nonzero irreducible L(K)-module.\",\"parameters\":[{\"symbol\":\"p\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"K\",\"type\":\"field\"},{\"symbol\":\"λ\",\"type\":\"integer\"},{\"symbol\":\"V\",\"type\":\"complex vector space equipped with a representation of sl₂(C), written V=V(λ)\"},{\"symbol\":\"x\",\"type\":\"complex-linear endomorphism of V\"},{\"symbol\":\"y\",\"type\":\"complex-linear endomorphism of V\"},{\"symbol\":\"h\",\"type\":\"complex-linear endomorphism of V\"},{\"symbol\":\"v\",\"type\":\"vector of V\"},{\"symbol\":\"M\",\"type\":\"additive subgroup of V\"}],\"hypotheses\":[{\"id\":\"H001\",\"statement\":\"p is prime, K has characteristic p, and 0≤λ<p.\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:16-17\"},{\"id\":\"H002\",\"statement\":\"V=V(λ) is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl₂(C)-module of highest weight λ and complex dimension λ+1. The Chevalley generator endomorphisms satisfy hx-xh=2x, hy-yh=-2y, and xy-yx=h.\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:18-24\"},{\"id\":\"H003\",\"statement\":\"v≠0, xv=0, and hv=λv.\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:26-27\"},{\"id\":\"H004\",\"statement\":\"M is an admissible lattice: it is a free abelian subgroup of V admitting an integer basis that is also a complex basis of V, and is stable under U_Z. The choice of M is arbitrary, not restricted to the minimal lattice.\",\"origin\":\"problem.md:30-32\"}],\"definitions\":[{\"id\":\"D001\",\"symbol\":\"n\",\"type\":\"positive integer, used as a natural number\",\"definition\":\"n=λ+1.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[\"H001\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"λ\"]},{\"id\":\"D002\",\"symbol\":\"I\",\"type\":\"finite set of natural-number indices\",\"definition\":\"I={i∈N:0≤i≤λ}; it has n elements.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D001\"],\"requires\":[\"H001\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"natural number\"}],\"objects\":[\"λ\",\"n\",\"i\"]},{\"id\":\"D003\",\"symbol\":\"e\",\"type\":\"family I→V\",\"definition\":\"For every i∈I, e_i=y^i v/i!, with 0!=1 and powers acting by composition.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D002\"],\"requires\":[\"H001\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"y\",\"v\",\"i\"]},{\"id\":\"D004\",\"symbol\":\"X\",\"type\":\"family of complex-linear endomorphisms of V indexed by natural numbers\",\"definition\":\"For every integer r≥0, X_r=x^r/r!, including X_0=Id_V.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\"}],\"objects\":[\"x\",\"V\",\"r\"]},{\"id\":\"D005\",\"symbol\":\"Y\",\"type\":\"family of complex-linear endomorphisms of V indexed by natural numbers\",\"definition\":\"For every integer r≥0, Y_r=y^r/r!, including Y_0=Id_V.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\"}],\"objects\":[\"y\",\"V\",\"r\"]},{\"id\":\"D006\",\"symbol\":\"U_Z\",\"type\":\"integer subalgebra of the universal enveloping algebra acting on V\",\"definition\":\"U_Z is the integer subalgebra of the universal enveloping algebra of sl₂(C) generated by X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r! for all integers r≥0; its action on V is the given representation extended to the enveloping algebra.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D004\",\"D005\"],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\"}],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"r\"]},{\"id\":\"D007\",\"symbol\":\"R\",\"type\":\"subring of Q, embedded in C\",\"definition\":\"R=Z_(p)={a/b∈Q:a,b∈Z and p does not divide b}, with operations inherited from Q. A unit of R means an element having a multiplicative inverse in R.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[\"H001\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"integer\"},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"integer\"}],\"objects\":[\"p\",\"a\",\"b\"]},{\"id\":\"D008\",\"symbol\":\"M_R\",\"type\":\"R-submodule of V\",\"definition\":\"M_R is the R-span of M in V, namely all finite sums of r_j m_j with r_j∈R and m_j∈M. The canonical map R⊗_Z M→M_R sends r⊗m to rm; its injectivity is to be proved, not assumed.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D007\"],\"requires\":[\"H001\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"r_j\",\"type\":\"elements of R\"},{\"symbol\":\"m_j\",\"type\":\"elements of M\"}],\"objects\":[\"R\",\"M\",\"V\",\"r_j\",\"m_j\"]},{\"id\":\"D009\",\"symbol\":\"E\",\"type\":\"family I×I→End_C(V)\",\"definition\":\"For i,j∈I, E_ij is the unique complex-linear map with E_ij(e_k)=δ_jk e_i for all k∈I, where δ_jk is 1 if j=k and 0 otherwise. The basis assertion N001 is required for this definition.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D002\",\"D003\"],\"requires\":[\"H001\",\"N001\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"k\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"e\",\"V\",\"i\",\"j\",\"k\"]},{\"id\":\"D010\",\"symbol\":\"J_i\",\"type\":\"family of R-submodules of C indexed by I\",\"definition\":\"For each i∈I, J_i={c∈C:c e_i∈M_R}, with addition and R-action inherited from C.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D003\",\"D007\",\"D008\"],\"requires\":[\"H001\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"complex number\"}],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"e\",\"M_R\",\"R\",\"i\",\"c\"]},{\"id\":\"D011\",\"symbol\":\"J\",\"type\":\"R-submodule of C\",\"definition\":\"J=J_0.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D010\"],\"requires\":[\"H001\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"J_i\"]},{\"id\":\"D012\",\"symbol\":\"V(K)\",\"type\":\"K-vector space\",\"definition\":\"V(K)=M⊗_Z K. Here tensor products have their usual balanced-module meaning: they are generated by pure tensors subject to additivity in each argument and (am)⊗c=m⊗(ac) for the base scalar a. Induced lattice endomorphisms act on the M factor; the same symbols x,y,h denote these induced K-linear operators once preservation of M is established.\",\"depends_on\":[],\"requires\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"M\",\"K\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\"]},{\"id\":\"D013\",\"symbol\":\"L(K)\",\"type\":\"K-Lie algebra acting on V(K)\",\"definition\":\"L(K)=(Zx+Zy+Zh)⊗_Z K with the bracket induced by commutators and the action induced from the lattice operators. This is the Chevalley construction, including in characteristic 2.\",\"depends_on\":[\"D012\"],\"requires\":[\"H002\",\"H004\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"K\",\"V(K)\"]}],\"logic\":{\"classical\":true,\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\",\"case_elimination\",\"natural_induction\",\"contradiction_classical\"]},\"pins\":{},\"inputs\":[]},\"graph\":{\"format_version\":2,\"case_id\":\"lie-module-irreducibility\",\"spec_sha256\":\"controller-bound\",\"propositions\":[{\"id\":\"H001\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"p\",\"K\",\"λ\"]},{\"id\":\"H002\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"V\",\"λ\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\"]},{\"id\":\"H003\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"v\",\"x\",\"h\",\"λ\"]},{\"id\":\"H004\",\"kind\":\"hypothesis\",\"definitions\":[\"D006\"],\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"M\",\"V\",\"U_Z\"]},{\"id\":\"M001\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"Let A be a commutative semiring, B a semiring with an A-algebra structure, T an additive commutative monoid and A-module, and C an index type. For an A-basis d:C→T and c∈C, the canonical scalar-extension basis d.baseChange(B), a B-basis of B⊗_A T indexed by C, satisfies d.baseChange(B)(c)=1⊗d(c).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"commutative semiring\"},{\"symbol\":\"B\",\"type\":\"semiring with A-algebra structure\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"additive commutative monoid and A-module\"},{\"symbol\":\"C\",\"type\":\"index type\"},{\"symbol\":\"d\",\"type\":\"A-basis of T indexed by C\"},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"element of C\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"T\",\"C\",\"d\",\"c\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Module.Basis.baseChange_apply\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A is a commutative semiring; B is a semiring with an A-algebra structure.\",\"T is an additive commutative monoid and an A-module.\",\"d is an A-basis of T indexed by C, and c∈C.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M002\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For a semiring A satisfying the strong rank condition, an additive commutative monoid T with an A-module structure, a finite index type C, and an A-basis d of T indexed by C, finrank_A(T)=card(C). Here finrank is the natural-valued module rank, and the strong rank condition says an injective A-linear map A^u→A^v forces u≤v for finite natural u,v.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"semiring satisfying the strong rank condition\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"additive commutative monoid and A-module\"},{\"symbol\":\"C\",\"type\":\"finite index type\"},{\"symbol\":\"d\",\"type\":\"A-basis of T indexed by C\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"T\",\"C\",\"d\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Module.finrank_eq_card_basis\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A is a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition.\",\"T is an additive commutative monoid and A-module.\",\"C is a finite index type and d is an A-basis of T indexed by C.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M003\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For a division ring A and an additive commutative group T with A-module structure which is finite-dimensional, a finite index type C, and a family d:C→T, if d is A-linearly independent and card(C)=finrank_A(T), then span_A(range d)=T.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"division ring\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"finite-dimensional A-module with additive commutative group\"},{\"symbol\":\"C\",\"type\":\"finite index type\"},{\"symbol\":\"d\",\"type\":\"family C→T\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"T\",\"C\",\"d\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"LinearIndependent.span_eq_top_of_card_eq_finrank'\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A is a division ring and T an additive commutative group with A-module structure.\",\"T is finite-dimensional over A and C is finite.\",\"d is A-linearly independent.\",\"card(C)=finrank_A(T).\"]}},{\"id\":\"M004\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"Let A and B be commutative semirings, S a multiplicative submonoid of A, and B an A-algebra which is a localization of A at S. Let T be an additive commutative monoid and A-module. Then the A-linear map f:T→B⊗_A T, f(t)=1⊗t, is a localized-module map at S: (i) multiplication by each s∈S on B⊗_A T is a unit in its ring of A-linear endomorphisms; (ii) for every z∈B⊗_A T there exist t∈T and s∈S with sz=f(t); (iii) f(t₁)=f(t₂) implies that st₁=st₂ for some s∈S. A localization B at S means the images of S are units, every element has a numerator in A and denominator in S, and equality of images of two elements of A is killed by some element of S.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"commutative semiring\"},{\"symbol\":\"B\",\"type\":\"commutative semiring and A-algebra\"},{\"symbol\":\"S\",\"type\":\"multiplicative submonoid of A\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"additive commutative monoid and A-module\"},{\"symbol\":\"f\",\"type\":\"A-linear map t↦1⊗t\"},{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"element of T\"},{\"symbol\":\"z\",\"type\":\"element of B⊗_A T\"},{\"symbol\":\"s\",\"type\":\"element of S\"},{\"symbol\":\"t₁\",\"type\":\"element of T\"},{\"symbol\":\"t₂\",\"type\":\"element of T\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"S\",\"T\",\"f\",\"t\",\"z\",\"s\",\"t₁\",\"t₂\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"IsLocalization.tensorProduct_isLocalizedModule\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A and B are commutative semirings, S is a multiplicative submonoid of A, and B is an A-algebra.\",\"B is a localization of A at S.\",\"T is an additive commutative monoid and A-module.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M005\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For a semiring A, additive commutative monoids T and U with A-module structures, and an A-linear equivalence f:T≃U, finrank_A(T)=finrank_A(U).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"semiring\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"additive commutative monoid and A-module\"},{\"symbol\":\"U\",\"type\":\"additive commutative monoid and A-module\"},{\"symbol\":\"f\",\"type\":\"A-linear equivalence T≃U\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"T\",\"U\",\"f\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"LinearEquiv.finrank_eq\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A is a semiring and T,U are additive commutative monoids with A-module structures.\",\"f is an A-linear equivalence from T to U.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M006\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"Let A be a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition, C a finite index type, and T_c, for c∈C, additive commutative monoids with A-module structures, each free and finitely generated as an A-module. Then finrank_A(∏_{c∈C} T_c)=∑_{c∈C} finrank_A(T_c).\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"semiring satisfying the strong rank condition\"},{\"symbol\":\"C\",\"type\":\"finite index type\"},{\"symbol\":\"T_c\",\"type\":\"family of additive commutative monoids and A-modules indexed by C\"},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"element of C\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"T_c\",\"c\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Module.finrank_pi_fintype\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A is a semiring satisfying the strong rank condition.\",\"C is a finite index type.\",\"Every T_c is an additive commutative monoid and A-module, free and finitely generated.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M007\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"For natural numbers d and q, if q is prime, then q divides d! if and only if q≤d.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"d\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"q\",\"type\":\"natural number\"}],\"objects\":[\"d\",\"q\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Nat.Prime.dvd_factorial\",\"hypotheses\":[\"d and q are natural numbers and q is prime.\"]}},{\"id\":\"M008\",\"kind\":\"mathlib\",\"statement\":\"Every additive commutative group T equipped with a module structure over a division ring A is a free A-module.\",\"definitions\":[],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"division ring\"},{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"additive commutative group and A-module\"}],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"T\"],\"source\":{\"declaration\":\"Module.Free.of_divisionRing\",\"hypotheses\":[\"A is a division ring and T is an additive commutative group with an A-module structure.\"]}},{\"id\":\"N001\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"e=(e_i)_{i∈I} is a complex basis of V. For every integer t≥0, hy^t v=(λ-2t)y^t v; for t≥1, xy^t v=t(λ-t+1)y^{t-1}v. Also y^{λ+1}v=0 and all higher powers on v vanish. On the basis, xe_0=0, xe_i=(λ-i+1)e_{i-1} for i≥1, ye_i=(i+1)e_{i+1} for i<λ, ye_λ=0, and he_i=(λ-2i)e_i. For all natural r and i∈I, X_r e_i=binom(λ-i+r,r)e_{i-r} if r≤i, and zero otherwise; Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_{i+r} if i+r≤λ, and zero otherwise. All displayed divided-power coefficients are integers.\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\"}],\"objects\":[\"e\",\"I\",\"V\",\"λ\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"v\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"t\",\"i\",\"r\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:45-84, with induction and basis details supplied\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"The map R⊗_Z M→M_R, r⊗m↦rm, is an R-linear isomorphism, M_R has an R-basis indexed by I, and its complex span is V. Each X_r and Y_r for r≥0 preserves M_R. For all i,j∈I, binom(λ,j) is a unit in R, and E_ij=binom(λ,j)^{-1} X_{λ-i}(Y_λ X_λ)Y_{λ-j}. In particular every E_ij preserves M_R. More explicitly Y_λX_λ=E_{λλ}, X_{λ-i}E_{λλ}=E_{iλ}, and E_{λλ}Y_{λ-j}=binom(λ,j)E_{λj}.\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D007\",\"D008\",\"D009\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"m\",\"type\":\"element of M\"},{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"R\",\"M\",\"M_R\",\"I\",\"V\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"E\",\"λ\",\"r\",\"m\",\"i\",\"j\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:86-116\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"For all i∈I, J_i=J; J is nonzero and finitely generated over R; M_R=⊕_{i∈I} J e_i inside V. The multiplication map Q⊗_R J→C, q⊗c↦qc, is injective and dim_Q(Q⊗_R J)=1. There exists b∈J with b≠0 and J=Rb, and for every such b, (b e_i)_{i∈I} is an R-basis of M_R.\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D007\",\"D008\",\"D010\",\"D011\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"q\",\"type\":\"rational number\"},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"element of J\"},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"element of J\"}],\"objects\":[\"J_i\",\"J\",\"I\",\"M_R\",\"e\",\"R\",\"V\",\"i\",\"q\",\"c\",\"b\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:118-148; rank-one tensor argument retained\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"kind\":\"internal\",\"statement\":\"The integer map Z→K extends to a ring map R→K by a/d↦(a in K)/(d in K). There are natural K-linear isomorphisms M⊗_Z K≃M_R⊗_R K≃(M_R/pM_R)⊗_{F_p}K, where F_p=Z/pZ and its map to K is induced by the integer map. There exists a K-basis β=(β_i)_{i∈I} of V(K), arising as the scalar extensions of b e_i for a nonzero b∈J with J=Rb, on which xβ_0=0, xβ_i=(λ-i+1)β_{i-1} for i≥1, yβ_i=(i+1)β_{i+1} for i<λ, yβ_λ=0, hβ_i=(λ-2i)β_i, with integer coefficients read in K. For every such basis define ε_ij by ε_ij β_k=δ_jk β_i. All binom(λ,j) and all r! for 0≤r≤λ are nonzero in K; induced divided powers satisfy X_r=(r!)^{-1}x^r and Y_r=(r!)^{-1}y^r in that range, and ε_ij=binom(λ,j)^{-1} X_{λ-i}(Y_λX_λ)Y_{λ-j}. Thus every K-subspace invariant under x,y is invariant under every ε_ij.\",\"definitions\":[\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D007\",\"D008\",\"D011\",\"D012\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"integer\"},{\"symbol\":\"d\",\"type\":\"integer with p not dividing d\"},{\"symbol\":\"β\",\"type\":\"K-basis indexed by I\"},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"element of J\"},{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"k\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"family of K-linear endomorphisms indexed by I×I\"},{\"symbol\":\"F_p\",\"type\":\"field Z/pZ\"}],\"objects\":[\"R\",\"K\",\"p\",\"M\",\"M_R\",\"V(K)\",\"I\",\"e\",\"J\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"λ\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"a\",\"d\",\"β\",\"b\",\"i\",\"j\",\"k\",\"r\",\"ε\",\"F_p\"],\"origin\":\"problem.md:150-170\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"kind\":\"target\",\"definitions\":[\"D012\",\"D013\"],\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"W\",\"type\":\"K-linear subspace of V(K)\"}],\"objects\":[\"V(K)\",\"K\",\"W\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"L(K)\"]}],\"inferences\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\",\"M003\"],\"output\":\"N001\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"natural_induction\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"natural number\",\"scope\":\"R001/S001\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S001\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Use t as the induction index for the formulas on y^t v, beginning at t=0.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"y\",\"v\"]},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"family I→C\",\"scope\":\"R001/S002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary complex coefficients c indexed by I to test a linear relation.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"H001 gives n>0 and the finite index set I. From H002 and H003, induction on t gives hy^t v=(λ-2t)y^t v and, for t≥1, xy^t v=t(λ-t+1)y^{t-1}v. Indeed h y=y h-2y gives the h step. For x, the base is xyv=yxv+hv=λv; if xy^t v=t(λ-t+1)y^{t-1}v, then xy^{t+1}v=yxy^t v+hy^t v=[t(λ-t+1)+λ-2t]y^t v=(t+1)(λ-t)y^t v. The t=0 h identity is hv=λv. Iterating the x identity, for 0≤i≤λ, gives x^i y^i v=i! λ(λ-1)⋯(λ-i+1)v≠0: every factor is a positive integer when i>0, and the empty product is 1 when i=0. Thus e_i≠0 for every i∈I.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H003\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\",\"I\",\"λ\",\"h\",\"x\",\"y\",\"v\",\"e\",\"t\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"For every t≥0, hy^t v=(λ-2t)y^t v, and for t≥1, xy^t v=t(λ-t+1)y^{t-1}v. Every e_i for i∈I is nonzero.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"natural number\"},{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"λ\",\"h\",\"x\",\"y\",\"v\",\"e\",\"I\",\"t\",\"i\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Take arbitrary c:I→C and temporarily assume L1: ∑_{i∈I} c_i e_i=0. For each j∈I, apply ∏_{k∈I,k≠j}(h-(λ-2k)Id_V). F001 makes every summand except the j-th vanish, leaving c_j ∏_{k≠j}2(k-j)e_j=0. Its vector and scalar factors are nonzero over C, so c_j=0. Discharge L1; the family e is linearly independent. H002 gives dim_C V=n=card(I), so M003 makes its span all of V. Independence and spanning are precisely the basis conditions. The h formula at t=λ+1 has eigenvalue -λ-2. Expanding y^{λ+1}v in this basis and comparing coefficients in h gives [-λ-2-(λ-2i)] times its i-th coefficient equal to zero. These multipliers are nonzero for all i∈I, hence y^{λ+1}v=0. Further powers vanish by applying y.\",\"uses\":[\"H002\",\"M003\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"c\",\"I\",\"h\",\"λ\",\"V\",\"e\",\"n\",\"y\",\"v\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"e is a complex basis of V, and y^{λ+1}v and every higher y-power on v vanish.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"e\",\"V\",\"y\",\"λ\",\"v\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\"],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Divide the identities in F001 by i! and use F002 to obtain xe_0=0, xe_i=(λ-i+1)e_{i-1} for i≥1, ye_i=(i+1)e_{i+1} for i<λ, ye_λ=0, and he_i=(λ-2i)e_i. For any r≥0, iterate these formulas r times and divide by r!: for r≤i the x coefficient is (λ-i+1)⋯(λ-i+r)/r!=binom(λ-i+r,r), and for i+r≤λ the y coefficient is (i+1)⋯(i+r)/r!=binom(i+r,r). Outside those ranges the string has already hit zero, so the result is zero. These binomial coefficients are integers (for example their usual counting interpretation as r-element subsets of a finite set proves integrality). At r=0 both products equal 1. This proves every clause of N001.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"λ\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"e\",\"X\",\"Y\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M003\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"A=C, T=V, C=I, d=e.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"C is a field and V a complex vector space by the parameter types.\",\"H002 gives finite dimension n and H001 gives I finite.\",\"The polynomial isolation argument earlier in S002 proves linear independence from F001.\",\"H002 and D001-D002 give card(I)=λ+1=dim_C(V).\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H004\",\"N001\",\"M001\",\"M002\",\"M007\"],\"output\":\"N002\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D007\",\"D008\",\"D009\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"exists_elimination\",\"forall_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"A\",\"type\":\"finite index set\",\"scope\":\"R002/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose a finite index set A for an integer basis of M which is also a complex basis of V, as supplied by admissibility H004; finite dimensionality is supplied by the basis N001.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H004\",\"N001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"M\",\"V\"]},{\"symbol\":\"m\",\"type\":\"family A→M\",\"scope\":\"R002/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose the corresponding integer basis m of M which is also a complex basis of V.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H004\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"M\",\"V\"]},{\"symbol\":\"Qop\",\"type\":\"complex-linear endomorphism of V\",\"scope\":\"R002/S003-S004\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define Qop=Y_λ X_λ; this is the projector denoted P in the supplied proof, renamed to avoid collision with the target ID.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"Y\",\"λ\",\"V\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"By H004 choose an integer basis m indexed by A which is also a complex basis. It is finite because V has the finite basis N001. M002 over C gives card(A)=dim_C V=card(I)=n. Reindexing by a bijection therefore permits an I-indexed basis. M001, with scalar extension Z→R, gives an R-basis (1⊗m_a) of R⊗_Z M. The multiplication map r⊗m↦rm sends this basis to the same vectors m_a in V. Their complex independence implies R-independence, and their R-span is M_R by definition. Thus this map is injective and onto M_R, and the images form an R-basis with n elements, reindexed by I.\",\"uses\":[\"H004\",\"N001\",\"M001\",\"M002\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"A\",\"m\",\"M\",\"V\",\"I\",\"n\",\"R\",\"M_R\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"The canonical map R⊗_Z M→M_R is an R-linear isomorphism, M_R has a basis indexed by I, and its complex span is V.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"R\",\"M\",\"M_R\",\"I\",\"V\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Every X_r and Y_r preserves M by H004 and D006. By complex linearity, it preserves the R-span M_R. Also M_R contains the basis vectors m_a, so its complex span is V, as recorded in F001. These statements do not restrict M to the minimal lattice.\",\"uses\":[\"H004\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"Y\",\"M\",\"M_R\",\"R\",\"m\",\"A\",\"V\",\"U_Z\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"For every natural r, X_r(M_R)⊆M_R and Y_r(M_R)⊆M_R.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\"}],\"objects\":[\"X\",\"Y\",\"M_R\",\"r\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Define Qop=Y_λ X_λ. Test N001 on every e_k: X_λ kills k<λ and sends e_λ to e_0, while Y_λ e_0=e_λ; hence Qop=E_{λλ}. Likewise X_{λ-i}Qop=E_{iλ}, since X_{λ-i}e_λ=e_i. Finally Qop Y_{λ-j}=binom(λ,j)E_{λj}: an input e_k with k<j lands below e_λ and is killed by Qop; one with k>j passes the end of the y-string and vanishes; at k=j the coefficient is binom(λ,λ-j)=binom(λ,j). These identities hold for all i,j∈I, including λ=0.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"Qop\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"λ\",\"E\",\"e\",\"I\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"Qop=E_{λλ}, X_{λ-i}Qop=E_{iλ}, and Qop Y_{λ-j}=binom(λ,j)E_{λj} for every i,j∈I.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"Qop\",\"E\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"λ\",\"I\",\"i\",\"j\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"For every j∈I, H001 and M007 show p divides none of λ!, j!, (λ-j)!. These integers therefore have inverses in R by its denominator definition. The identity binom(λ,j)=λ!/(j!(λ-j)!) makes this binomial a unit in R. Composing F003 gives X_{λ-i}Qop Y_{λ-j}=binom(λ,j)E_ij, whence E_ij=binom(λ,j)^{-1}X_{λ-i}(Y_λX_λ)Y_{λ-j}. F002 and closure of the R-module M_R under R-scalars prove preservation by every E_ij. F001 supplies the other assertions of N002. No reduced h-eigenvalue argument has been used.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"M007\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\",\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"p\",\"λ\",\"I\",\"R\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"Qop\",\"E\",\"M_R\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M001\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"A=Z, B=R, T=M, C=the local finite index set A, d=m.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Z and R are commutative rings with the inclusion Z→R; H001 ensures R is the localization subring D007.\",\"The additive subgroup M is a Z-module.\",\"H004 supplies exactly the chosen integer basis m; the formula applies at every index of A.\"]},{\"input\":\"M002\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"Source A=C (complex numbers), T=V, C=local index set A, d=m viewed as the complex basis from H004.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"C is a field, hence satisfies the strong rank condition.\",\"V is a complex vector space.\",\"The chosen family m is a complex basis by H004 and is finite since V has the finite basis N001.\"]},{\"input\":\"M007\",\"at\":\"S004\",\"bindings\":\"q=p and d successively λ, j, λ-j, for every j∈I.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"H001 makes p prime; all three d are natural numbers strictly below p because 0≤j≤λ<p.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"N001\",\"N002\",\"M001\",\"M002\",\"M003\",\"M004\",\"M005\",\"M006\",\"M008\"],\"output\":\"N003\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D007\",\"D008\",\"D009\",\"D010\",\"D011\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"exists_elimination\",\"natural_induction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"T\",\"type\":\"Q-vector space\",\"scope\":\"R003/S002-S006\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define T=Q⊗_R J.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"R\",\"J\"]},{\"symbol\":\"μ\",\"type\":\"Q-linear map T→C\",\"scope\":\"R003/S002-S006\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define μ(q⊗c)=qc, extending linearly by tensor balancing.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"T\",\"J\",\"R\"]},{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"natural number\",\"scope\":\"R003/S003-S006\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define r=finrank_Q T.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"T\"]},{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"element of J\",\"scope\":\"R003/S004-S006\",\"start\":\"S004\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose a≠0 in J, using its nonzeroness in F001.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"J\"]},{\"symbol\":\"k\",\"type\":\"positive natural number\",\"scope\":\"R003/S004-S006\",\"start\":\"S004\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose the length k≥1 of a finite list of nonzero R-generators of J, discarding zero generators.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"J\"]},{\"symbol\":\"g\",\"type\":\"family {1,...,k}→J\",\"scope\":\"R003/S004-S006\",\"start\":\"S004\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose nonzero generators g_1,...,g_k of J from F001.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"J\",\"k\"]},{\"symbol\":\"q\",\"type\":\"family {1,...,k}→Q\",\"scope\":\"R003/S005-S006\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose the nonzero rational coefficients q_j with g_j=q_j a established in F004.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"g\",\"a\",\"k\"]},{\"symbol\":\"νs\",\"type\":\"family {1,...,k}→Z\",\"scope\":\"R003/S006\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose integer exponents νs_j in the factorizations of F005.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F005\"],\"objects\":[\"q\",\"k\",\"p\"]},{\"symbol\":\"u\",\"type\":\"family {1,...,k}→R\",\"scope\":\"R003/S006\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose units u_j∈R with q_j=p^{νs_j}u_j as in F005.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F005\"],\"objects\":[\"q\",\"νs\",\"k\",\"p\",\"R\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ν\",\"type\":\"integer\",\"scope\":\"R003/S006\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define ν=min_{1≤j≤k} νs_j, which exists since k≥1.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F005\"],\"objects\":[\"νs\",\"k\"]},{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"complex number\",\"scope\":\"R003/S006\",\"start\":\"S006\",\"end\":\"S006\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define b=p^ν a, interpreting the integer power in Q⊂C.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"p\",\"ν\",\"a\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"For i∈I, E_ii maps M_R onto J_i e_i: its image is contained there by N002 and the coordinate formula, and it fixes every vector c e_i in that module. For i,j∈I, applying E_ij to c e_j proves J_j⊆J_i; interchanging indices proves equality. Thus J_i=J_0=J. Every vector in M_R is the sum of its E_ii projections, and the independence of e in N001 makes this sum direct. Therefore M_R=⊕_{i∈I}J e_i. Each summand is generated by the projections of the finite basis in N002. Since e_i≠0, multiplication by e_i identifies J with this summand, so J is finitely generated. J cannot be zero: otherwise M_R=0 would contradict its complex span being V and the nonzero basis N001 with n>0 from H001.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"N001\",\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"E\",\"M_R\",\"J_i\",\"J\",\"e\",\"V\",\"n\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"J_i=J for all i∈I; J is a nonzero finitely generated R-submodule of C, and M_R=⊕_{i∈I}J e_i.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"J_i\",\"J\",\"R\",\"M_R\",\"e\",\"I\",\"i\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Define T=Q⊗_R J and μ:T→C by μ(q⊗c)=qc; balancing makes this a Q-linear map. Q is a localization of R at its nonzero elements: nonzero elements become units, every rational is a numerator/denominator with both in R (indeed integers suffice), and equality in Q is equality in the subring R, so the equality-killing condition holds with 1. M004 then says every z∈T satisfies sz=1⊗c for some c∈J and nonzero s∈R. Consequently μ(z)=c/s. If μ(z)=0, then c=0 in C, hence in J, so sz=0 and z=0 since s is invertible over Q. Thus μ is injective and its image is exactly the rational span of J. A finite R-generating list of J from F001 gives a finite Q-spanning list of T, because z=s^{-1}(1⊗c) and c is an R-combination of that list. Hence T is finite-dimensional.\",\"uses\":[\"M004\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"T\",\"μ\",\"R\",\"J\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"T is finite-dimensional over Q and μ:T→C is injective with image span_Q J.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"T\",\"μ\",\"J\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Define r=finrank_Q T. Tensoring the direct decomposition F001 yields a Q-linear equivalence Q⊗_R M_R≃∏_{i∈I}T. Explicitly, on a pure tensor q₀⊗m, take its i-th coordinate to be q₀⊗c_i, where m=∑ c_i e_i with c_i∈J. The inverse takes a tuple whose entries are finite sums of q⊗c to the sum of the tensors q⊗(c e_i). Coordinate extraction is R-linear; these prescriptions are balanced and additive, and their composites fix pure tensors and tuples of pure tensors, hence all finite sums, so they are inverse. M001 applied to the I-indexed R-basis of M_R supplied by N002 gives an I-indexed Q-basis of Q⊗_R M_R; M002 gives its dimension n. M008 gives freeness of T over Q, while F002 gives finite generation. Thus M006 gives dimension of ∏_I T equal to ∑_I r=nr, and M005 applied to the displayed equivalence gives n=nr. Since n=λ+1>0 by H001, r=1.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"N002\",\"M001\",\"M002\",\"M005\",\"M006\",\"M008\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"r\",\"T\",\"R\",\"M_R\",\"I\",\"J\",\"e\",\"n\",\"λ\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"finrank_Q T=1, with T finite-dimensional and μ injective.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"T\",\"μ\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"By F001 choose 0≠a∈J and a finite nonzero generating list g_1,...,g_k of J, with k≥1. The vector 1⊗a in T is nonzero because its μ-image is a. Thus this singleton is Q-linearly independent (a scalar multiple equal to zero has scalar zero). F003 and M003 show that it spans T. For each 1≤j≤k, write 1⊗g_j as q_j(1⊗a) and apply μ to get g_j=q_j a. Since g_j≠0, q_j≠0. In particular all generators lie in the one-dimensional rational line Q a; this conclusion uses the rank computation, not merely the inclusion J⊂C.\",\"uses\":[\"M003\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\",\"F003\"],\"objects\":[\"a\",\"g\",\"k\",\"J\",\"T\",\"μ\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F004\",\"statement\":\"There exists a family q of nonzero rational numbers indexed by {1,...,k} such that g_j=q_j a for every 1≤j≤k.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"q\",\"type\":\"family {1,...,k}→Q\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"integer between 1 and k\"}],\"objects\":[\"q\",\"g\",\"a\",\"k\",\"j\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S005\",\"text\":\"Choose the family q from F004. Each nonzero rational q_j can be written p^{ν_j}u_j with ν_j∈Z and u_j a unit in R. To see existence without assuming a rank-one ideal theorem, write the rational as a ratio of two nonzero integers. For a positive integer d, divide off p repeatedly while it divides d. This terminates: p≥2 by H001, so each division of a positive divisible integer strictly decreases it; equivalently induction on d supplies a largest nonnegative exponent with remaining positive factor not divisible by p. Apply this to the absolute values of numerator and denominator; keep their signs in the remaining factors. Subtract the two exponents to get ν_j. The remaining ratio and its inverse both have denominators not divisible by p, hence belong to R, giving the unit u_j. Applying this finite construction to all indices gives the families in F005.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F004\"],\"objects\":[\"q\",\"g\",\"k\",\"p\",\"R\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F005\",\"statement\":\"There exist integer exponents νs_j and units u_j∈R, for 1≤j≤k, with q_j=p^{νs_j}u_j.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"νs\",\"type\":\"family {1,...,k}→Z\"},{\"symbol\":\"u\",\"type\":\"family {1,...,k}→R consisting of units\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"integer between 1 and k\"}],\"objects\":[\"νs\",\"u\",\"q\",\"p\",\"R\",\"k\",\"j\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S006\",\"text\":\"Choose νs and u from F005; let ν be their finite minimum and set b=p^ν a≠0. For every j, g_j=q_j a=p^{νs_j-ν}u_j b∈Rb, since νs_j-ν≥0. Conversely an index attaining the minimum gives g_j=u_j b, so b=u_j^{-1}g_j∈J. Thus J=Rb. This proves the required existential statement. For any nonzero b∈J with J=Rb, F001 gives spanning of M_R by (b e_i), and N001 gives their R-independence: a relation divided by the nonzero complex scalar b is a relation on e. Hence they form an R-basis. F001, F002 and F003 provide all remaining assertions of N003, including injectivity of the tensor multiplication map and dimension one.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\",\"F002\",\"F003\",\"F004\",\"F005\"],\"objects\":[\"νs\",\"u\",\"ν\",\"b\",\"p\",\"a\",\"q\",\"g\",\"k\",\"J\",\"R\",\"M_R\",\"I\",\"e\",\"T\",\"μ\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M004\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"A=R, S=R\\\\{0}, B=Q, source T=J, and f(c)=1⊗c.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"R⊂Q is a commutative ring by H001 and D007; its nonzero elements form a multiplicative submonoid since it is a domain, and Q is its commutative algebra.\",\"The numerator, denominator and equality conditions are verified explicitly earlier in S002 using R⊂Q and integer fractions.\",\"J is an R-submodule of C by D011; it is an additive commutative group and R-module.\"]},{\"input\":\"M001\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"A=R, B=Q, source T=M_R, C=I, and d any I-indexed R-basis supplied by N002.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"R and Q are commutative rings with the inclusion algebra structure.\",\"M_R is an R-submodule of V by D008.\",\"N002 supplies the I-indexed basis, and the formula applies for every i∈I.\"]},{\"input\":\"M002\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"A=Q, source T=Q⊗_R M_R, C=I and d the scalar-extension basis delivered by M001.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Q is a field, hence satisfies the strong rank condition.\",\"The tensor product is a Q-vector space.\",\"M001 earlier in S003 supplies the basis; I is finite with card(I)=n by H001 and D002.\"]},{\"input\":\"M005\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"A=Q, source T=Q⊗_R M_R, U=∏_{i∈I}T, f=the coordinate tensor equivalence displayed in S003.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Both sides are Q-vector spaces.\",\"The maps are explicitly balanced linear maps, with inverse composites checked on generators earlier in S003.\"]},{\"input\":\"M006\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"A=Q, C=I, and every component T_c equal to the local space T=Q⊗_R J.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Q is a field and satisfies the strong rank condition.\",\"I is finite with n indices.\",\"T is a Q-vector space; M008 earlier in S003 gives freeness and F002 gives finite generation by a finite spanning list.\"]},{\"input\":\"M008\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"A=Q, source T=local T.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Q is a division ring and T=Q⊗_R J is a Q-vector space with additive commutative group.\"]},{\"input\":\"M003\",\"at\":\"S004\",\"bindings\":\"A=Q, source T=local T, C=a singleton, d its sole vector 1⊗a.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"T is a Q-vector space.\",\"F002 gives finite dimension, and a singleton is finite.\",\"The μ-image of 1⊗a is nonzero a, so the singleton is independent by field scalar cancellation.\",\"Its cardinality is 1, equal to dim_Q T by F003.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H004\",\"N001\",\"N002\",\"N003\",\"M001\",\"M007\"],\"output\":\"N004\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D003\",\"D004\",\"D005\",\"D006\",\"D007\",\"D008\",\"D009\",\"D011\",\"D012\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"exists_elimination\",\"forall_introduction\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"b\",\"type\":\"element of J\",\"scope\":\"R004/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose b≠0 in J with J=Rb, using N003.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N003\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"J\",\"R\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ρ\",\"type\":\"ring homomorphism R→K\",\"scope\":\"R004/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define ρ(a/d)=(a in K)/(d in K) for p not dividing d; well-definedness is established in S001.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"R\",\"K\",\"p\"]},{\"symbol\":\"F_p\",\"type\":\"field\",\"scope\":\"R004/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define F_p=Z/pZ with its natural map to K.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"H001\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"p\",\"K\"]},{\"symbol\":\"β\",\"type\":\"family I→V(K)\",\"scope\":\"R004/S003-S004\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define β_i to be the image of (b e_i)⊗1 under the inverse of the first isomorphism constructed in S002.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N003\"],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"b\",\"e\",\"I\",\"K\",\"V(K)\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"family I×I→End_K(V(K))\",\"scope\":\"R004/S003-S004\",\"start\":\"S003\",\"end\":\"S004\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"After establishing in S003 that β is a basis, define ε_ij by ε_ij β_k=δ_jk β_i.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\",\"β\",\"V(K)\",\"K\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Choose b as in N003. Since K has characteristic p by H001, the kernel of Z→K is pZ: Euclidean division by p reduces any integer to a remainder 0≤s<p, and the definition of characteristic says no positive such remainder maps to zero. Consequently any integer d not divisible by p has nonzero image in K. Define ρ(a/d)=a_K/d_K on R. Equality of fractions is cross-multiplication in Z, hence in K; their denominators remain nonzero, proving well-definedness, additivity and multiplicativity. Thus ρ extends the integer map. Its kernel is pR, since a/d maps to zero exactly when p divides a. Reduction sends a/d modulo p to a times the inverse of d in F_p=Z/pZ, giving R/pR≃F_p with the natural inclusion F_p→K. The latter is injective by the same characteristic argument. Also X_1=x and Y_1=y preserve M by H004; H002 gives h=xy-yx, so h preserves M too. All induced lattice actions in D012 are therefore defined.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H004\",\"N003\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"b\",\"J\",\"R\",\"ρ\",\"K\",\"p\",\"F_p\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"M\",\"U_Z\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F000\",\"statement\":\"ρ:R→K is a well-defined ring map extending Z→K with kernel pR, and R/pR≃F_p=Z/pZ compatibly with the natural injection F_p→K. The operators x,y,h preserve M.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"ρ\",\"R\",\"K\",\"p\",\"F_p\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"M\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Use N002 to identify M_R with R⊗_Z M. The first isomorphism sends m⊗c in M⊗_Z K to m⊗c in M_R⊗_R K, equivalently (1⊗m)⊗c. Its inverse sends (r⊗m)⊗c to m⊗ρ(r)c. Integer and R-balancing verify both maps, and their composites fix every pure tensor, hence all finite sums. For the second isomorphism send u⊗c to (u+pM_R)⊗c. The inverse sends (u+pM_R)⊗c to u⊗c; changing u by pz changes the result by z⊗pc=0. Balancing over F_p follows from F000 and the R-action through R/pR; the same pure tensor check shows inverse composites. These maps are K-linear and intertwine every induced R-linear lattice operator, as is checked on pure tensors.\",\"uses\":[\"N002\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F000\"],\"objects\":[\"M\",\"M_R\",\"R\",\"K\",\"p\",\"F_p\",\"ρ\",\"V(K)\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"There are K-linear isomorphisms V(K)=M⊗_Z K≃M_R⊗_R K≃(M_R/pM_R)⊗_{F_p}K with exactly the maps displayed in S002; they intertwine all induced lattice operators.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"V(K)\",\"M\",\"M_R\",\"K\",\"R\",\"p\",\"F_p\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"N003 says (b e_i) is an R-basis of M_R. Applying M001 with R→K makes the vectors 1⊗(b e_i) a K-basis of K⊗_R M_R. The flip of pure tensors, c⊗u↔u⊗c, is balanced and has itself as inverse, so it identifies this basis with (b e_i)⊗1 in M_R⊗_R K. Transporting through F001 defines β_i and proves β is a K-basis of V(K). Reduction of the R-basis modulo p is also a basis over F_p: its coordinates identify M_R with R^I and pM_R with (pR)^I, hence the quotient with (R/pR)^I. The second isomorphism in F001 therefore gives the same basis by reduction and extension. N001 applied to b e_i (b is a complex scalar) gives exactly xβ_0=0, xβ_i=(λ-i+1)β_{i-1}, yβ_i=(i+1)β_{i+1} for i<λ, yβ_λ=0, hβ_i=(λ-2i)β_i, with the boundary restrictions on x as in N001 and all coefficients mapped to K. Define ε_ij to be the matrix units for this basis. By N002, E_ij preserve M_R and hence induce these ε_ij, and their product identities persist by F001.\",\"uses\":[\"N001\",\"N002\",\"N003\",\"M001\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"b\",\"e\",\"I\",\"M_R\",\"R\",\"K\",\"ρ\",\"p\",\"F_p\",\"β\",\"V(K)\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"λ\",\"E\",\"ε\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"β is a K-basis of V(K) obtained from b e_i by the stated scalar-extension maps, with all x,y,h matrices in N004. The induced E_ij are ε_ij, and the identities of N002 hold for these induced operators with coefficients mapped by ρ.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"β\",\"V(K)\",\"K\",\"b\",\"e\",\"I\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"E\",\"ε\",\"ρ\",\"i\",\"j\"],\"assumptions\":[]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S004\",\"text\":\"For each 0≤r≤λ<p, M007 gives p not dividing r!, so its image in K is nonzero by F000. On the original lattice r!X_r=x^r and r!Y_r=y^r, and both sides preserve M. Thus after scalar extension X_r=(r!)^{-1}x^r and Y_r=(r!)^{-1}y^r in this range. N002 states binom(λ,j) is a unit in R; its image in K is a unit since ρ sends its inverse to an inverse. F002 therefore gives ε_ij=binom(λ,j)^{-1}X_{λ-i}(Y_λX_λ)Y_{λ-j}. A subspace invariant under x,y is invariant under their nonnegative powers, scalar multiples and compositions, so this formula proves its invariance under every ε_ij. All indices used here lie between 0 and λ. The argument works for any witness b allowed by N003, establishing every quantifier of N004.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"N002\",\"M007\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F000\",\"F001\",\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"λ\",\"p\",\"K\",\"R\",\"ρ\",\"I\",\"X\",\"Y\",\"x\",\"y\",\"M\",\"β\",\"ε\",\"b\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[]}],\"applications\":[{\"input\":\"M001\",\"at\":\"S003\",\"bindings\":\"A=R, B=K with algebra map ρ, T=M_R, C=I, d_i=b e_i.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"R and K are commutative rings and F000 proves the ring map ρ.\",\"M_R is an R-module by D008.\",\"N003 and the witness b from S001 give the R-basis d_i=b e_i.\"]},{\"input\":\"M007\",\"at\":\"S004\",\"bindings\":\"q=p, d=r for each natural 0≤r≤λ.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"H001 gives prime p and 0≤r≤λ<p, so the source equivalence excludes p dividing r!.\"]}]},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"inputs\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H004\",\"N004\"],\"output\":\"P\",\"definitions\":[\"D001\",\"D002\",\"D012\",\"D013\"],\"rules\":[\"direct\",\"forall_introduction\",\"implication_introduction\",\"case_elimination\",\"exists_elimination\"],\"locals\":[{\"symbol\":\"β\",\"type\":\"K-basis of V(K) indexed by I\",\"scope\":\"R005/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose the K-basis β with matrix-unit identities supplied by N004.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N004\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\",\"V(K)\",\"I\"]},{\"symbol\":\"ε\",\"type\":\"family I×I→End_K(V(K))\",\"scope\":\"R005/argument\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Define ε_ij to be the matrix units of the chosen basis β as in N004.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N004\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"β\",\"K\",\"V(K)\",\"I\"]},{\"symbol\":\"W\",\"type\":\"K-linear subspace of V(K)\",\"scope\":\"R005/S001-S003\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S003\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary K-linear subspace W of V(K).\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"K\",\"V(K)\"]},{\"symbol\":\"w\",\"type\":\"vector of W\",\"scope\":\"R005/S002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"In the nonzero branch choose w≠0 in W using F001 under L2.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"W\"]},{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"family I→K\",\"scope\":\"R005/S002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Let c be the unique coordinate family of w in the basis β.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"N004\"],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"β\",\"I\",\"K\"]},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\",\"scope\":\"R005/S002\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose j with c_j≠0; equivalently choose the index of a nonzero coordinate of w whose existence is in F001.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"β\",\"I\"]}],\"argument\":[{\"id\":\"S001\",\"text\":\"Choose β and define ε as in N004; H001 gives n=λ+1>0, so I is nonempty. The basis vector β_0 is nonzero, proving V(K)≠0. Fix an arbitrary subspace W and assume L1: W is invariant under x,y,h. N004 then makes W invariant under every ε_ij. If W={0}, the desired alternative is already true. In the other branch assume L2: W≠{0}. By this assumption W has a nonzero vector; since β is a basis, such a vector has a nonzero coordinate. Record F001 to choose both a vector and an index in the next paragraph.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"N004\"],\"uses_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"β\",\"ε\",\"I\",\"n\",\"λ\",\"V(K)\",\"K\",\"W\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"statement\":\"There exist a nonzero vector z∈W and an index t∈I such that the t-th coordinate of z in β is nonzero. Also W is invariant under every ε_ij.\",\"binders\":[{\"symbol\":\"z\",\"type\":\"vector in W\"},{\"symbol\":\"t\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"i\",\"type\":\"element of I\"},{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\"}],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"I\",\"β\",\"ε\",\"z\",\"t\",\"i\",\"j\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"]}],\"introduces\":[\"L1\",\"L2\"],\"discharges\":[]},{\"id\":\"S002\",\"text\":\"Choose the vector w and index j jointly from F001 and let w=∑_{i∈I}c_i β_i be its basis expansion, so c_j≠0. For every i∈I, the matrix-unit formula gives ε_ij w=c_j β_i∈W. Since K is a field, multiplication by c_j^{-1} gives β_i∈W. Every vector of V(K) is a K-linear combination of these basis vectors, so W=V(K). Thus in the nonzero branch the required alternative holds; discharge L2 and combine with the zero branch to get W={0} or W=V(K) under L1.\",\"uses\":[],\"uses_local\":[\"F001\"],\"objects\":[\"w\",\"c\",\"j\",\"β\",\"ε\",\"I\",\"W\",\"K\",\"V(K)\"],\"produces\":[{\"id\":\"F002\",\"statement\":\"W={0} or W=V(K).\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"V(K)\"],\"assumptions\":[\"L1\"]}],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L2\"]},{\"id\":\"S003\",\"text\":\"Discharge L1 and universally quantify the arbitrary W. Together with nonzeroness proved in S001 this proves the asserted subspace statement. For the Lie-algebra formulation, H004 and H002 give lattice preservation of x,y and h=xy-yx, so L(K) acts as defined; invariance under its generator span is equivalent, by linearity, to invariance under x,y,h. Hence the same statement is irreducibility as an L(K)-module. No algebraic closure of K was used. When λ=0, n=1 and all factorials and binomials in the route are 1; the proof remains valid. When p=2, H001 permits λ=0 or 1 and all factorials used have r<2. No distinctness of reduced h-eigenvalues was invoked.\",\"uses\":[\"H001\",\"H002\",\"H004\"],\"uses_local\":[\"F002\"],\"objects\":[\"W\",\"V(K)\",\"L(K)\",\"K\",\"M\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"λ\",\"p\",\"n\",\"I\",\"β\",\"ε\"],\"produces\":[],\"introduces\":[],\"discharges\":[\"L1\"]}],\"applications\":[]}]}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assu